module

public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedComplete.AdicDerivedCompletion.CompletionUnitIsIso

/-!
# Derived completion as a limit of Koszul complexes

For an ideal generated by a finite sequence, derived completion is computed functorially as the
derived inverse limit of the derived tensor products with the Koszul complexes on positive powers
of that sequence. This functor is left adjoint to the inclusion of derived-complete objects.

## Main definitions

* `AdicKoszulAdjunction.completionHomEquiv`: for a functor `completion` with values in a property
  `P` and a unit `𝟭 C ⟶ completion`, morphisms from a completion to an object of `P` are
  morphisms from the original object.
* `AdicKoszulAdjunction.reflectionOfCompletion`: such a completion is left adjoint to the
  inclusion of `P`.

## Main results

* `AdicKoszulAdjunction.completion_hom_bijective`: precomposition with the unit is a bijection.
* `AdicKoszulAdjunction.koszulPowerDerivedLimit_isLeftAdjoint`: the functor whose value at `K` is
  the derived limit of the tensor--Koszul tower of `K` is left adjoint to the inclusion of the
  derived-complete objects.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0920](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0920)
* [Bhatt--Scholze, *Projectivity of the Witt vector affine Grassmannian*][BS]
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

